    <section class="faq-section">
      <div class="section-container">
        <div class="section-header">
          <p class="section-label">Common Questions</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">Tree Trimming FAQ</h2>
          <p class="section-desc">Answers to questions Eau Claire homeowners ask before scheduling pruning work.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details class="faq-item" open>
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question-text">When is the best time to prune trees?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Most deciduous trees are best pruned during late winter or early spring when they're dormant — before new growth begins. Flowering trees should be pruned right after they bloom. We assess each tree individually and time the work accordingly.</p></div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question-text">How often should I have my trees trimmed?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Most residential trees benefit from pruning every 3-5 years. Fast-growing species may need attention more frequently. We'll assess your trees during the free assessment and give you a recommended schedule.</p></div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question-text">Can I trim my own trees?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Small ornamental trees and shrubs can sometimes be handled by homeowners. However, large tree pruning requires professional climbing equipment, proper training, and an understanding of tree biology. Improper cuts can harm the tree. When in doubt, call us.</p></div>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question-text">What does proper pruning cost?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Cost depends on the number and size of trees, their condition, and the type of work needed. We provide a free on-site estimate so you know the cost before we start. There's no obligation.</p></div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

